Scenario: View Homepage as Developer Services user
	Developer Services users should be able to view the Developer Services Quick Link.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved                   |
	| Name             | Frontend Org Name 1        |
	| Tags             | developer_services         |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                       |
	| Shared Comments  | true                       |
	| SLA              | Gold                       |
	| Tier             | T4                         |
	| Support Region   | US                         |
	| Support Language | English                    |
	| External ID      | 12341234                   |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name         | Zendesk Enduser1                    |
	| Tags         | osb_customer,osb_kb                 |
	| Password     | zendeskqauser                       |
	| Role         | End-user                            |
	| Access       | Organization                        |
	| Email        | zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number | +1 (555) 555-5555                   |
	| Organization | Frontend Org Name 1                 |
	| Language     | English                             |
	| Time Zone    | Pacific Time (US & Canada)          |
	| External ID  | Enduser1                            |
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I accept all cookies
	Then I should see the Developer Services link

Scenario: View Homepage as KB User
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	KB Users should only be able to view certain options available to KB Users.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved                   |
	| Name             | Frontend Org Name 1        |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp,liferay_portal |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                       |
	| Shared Comments  | true                       |
	| SLA              | Gold                       |
	| Tier             | T4                         |
	| Support Region   | US                         |
	| Support Language | English                    |
	| External ID      | 12341234                   |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name         | Zendesk Enduser1                    |
	| Tags         | osb_kb                              |
	| Password     | zendeskqauser                       |
	| Role         | End-user                            |
	| Access       | Organization                        |
	| Email        | zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number | +1 (555) 555-5555                   |
	| Organization | Frontend Org Name 1                 |
	| Language     | English                             |
	| Time Zone    | Pacific Time (US & Canada)          |
	| External ID  | Enduser1                            |
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I accept all cookies
	Then I should see the homepage as a kb user
	And the current language should be listed as "English (US)"
	And I should not see the Developer Services link

